{"name":"Lilac Paradise","hex":"#dcbbba","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lilac","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large shrub of the genus Syringa, especially Syringa vulgaris, bearing white, pale-pink, or purple flowers.","A flower of the lilac shrub."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Of a cat or its fur: having a pale brown colour, lighter than chocolate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lilac"},{"term":"paradise","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The place where sanctified souls are believed to live after death.","A very pleasant place, such as a place full of lush vegetation."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Paradise (“Heaven”).","Alternative letter-case form of Paradise (“the Garden of Eden”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paradise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Syringa","blocks":[{"text":"Syringa is a genus of 12 currently recognized species of flowering woody plants in the olive family known colloquially as lilacs. They are native to woodland and scrub from southeastern Europe to eastern Asia, and widely and commonly cultivated in temperate areas elsewhere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Stockholm-lilac.jpg/330px-Stockholm-lilac.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syringa","wikidata":"Q157449"},{"title":"Paradise","blocks":[{"text":"In religion and folklore, paradise is a place of everlasting happiness, delight, and bliss. Paradisiacal notions are often laden with pastoral imagery, and may be cosmogonical, eschatological, or both, often contrasted with the miseries of human civilization: in paradise there is only peace, prosperity, and happiness. Paradise is a place of contentment, a land of luxury and fulfillment containing ever-lasting bliss and delight. Paradise is often described as a \"higher place\", the holiest place, in contrast to this world, or underworlds such as hell."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Angelico%2C_giudizio_universale_01.jpg/330px-Angelico%2C_giudizio_universale_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paradise","wikidata":"Q3363340"},{"title":"Lilac (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lilac is a light shade of purple or violet representing the average color of most lilac flowers. The colors of some lilac flowers may be equivalent to the colors shown below as pale lilac, rich lilac, or deep lilac. However, there are other lilac flowers that are colored red-violet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Stockholm-lilac.jpg/330px-Stockholm-lilac.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilac_(color)","wikidata":"Q12894641"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Lilac_Bush.jpg/500px-Lilac_Bush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Lilac_Bush.jpg/1280px-Lilac_Bush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Lilac_Bush.jpg/500px-Lilac_Bush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Purple lilac bush","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALilac_Bush.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Lilac_buds.jpg/500px-Lilac_buds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Lilac_buds.jpg/500px-Lilac_buds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dormant lilac buds","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F